  "verbalization": "Schizopeptin 791 is shown to have targets that ultimately lead to DNA polymerase alpha subunit B through multiple distinct pathways. The first pathway involves Schizopeptin 791 targeting tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 8, which in turn is a target of a complex compound with DNA polymerase alpha subunit B as its final target. The second pathway involves Schizopeptin 791 targeting sphingosine 1-phosphate receptor 4, which is also a target of another compound that ultimately targets DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. The third pathway involves Schizopeptin 791 targeting sphingosine 1-phosphate receptor 4, which is a target of a different compound that also leads to DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. These findings suggest that Schizopeptin 791 may exert its biological effects through multiple distinct mechanisms, ultimately targeting DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. The evidence supports a potential role for Schizopeptin 791 in modulating DNA polymerase alpha subunit B activity, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
